CodeMirror Extended Syntax
==========================

Optional editor-only highlighting for the CosmoCode DokuWiki CodeMirror plugin
(2026 module-based version). No DokuWiki core, CodeMirror, or renderer changes.

All definitions live in this plugin's definitions.js, grouped by plugin name.
There are no files to install or maintain in the supported plugins themselves.
Each definition is an object with any of these fields:

  tags: ['figure', 'subfigure', 'caption']
  braces: ['ref', 'autoref']
  mediaExtensions: ['svg']
  tokens: [{match: /^@EXAMPLE@/, style: 'variable-2', sol: false}]
  blocks: [{open: /^\/\*/, close: '*/', style: 'comment', singleLine: false}]
  codeOptions: true

Patterns must match at the current position, consume at least one character,
and have no global/sticky flags. Tags and prefixes are case-sensitive; include
all supported spellings. Blocks protect their contents from wiki highlighting.
Styles are standard CodeMirror styles: tag, attribute, string, keyword, number,
operator, link, meta, comment, etc. The selected editor theme controls colours.

The loader only runs on editor pages and selects rules for installed, enabled
plugins from definitions.js. It does not infer syntax from their PHP code.
It handles asynchronous loading and editor/highlighting toggles through the
upstream codemirror_ready event. Disabling it leaves ordinary CodeMirror intact.

Supported plugins: approve, bootswrapper, codehighlightjs, datatables, diagrams,
gallery, icons, iframe, latexcaption, mathjax, pageredirect, qrcodephp, threejs.

This is a highlighter, not syntax validation or autocomplete. It never changes
the text that is saved. Update definitions.js here when adding custom syntax.
Code/file/nowiki and embedded language contents retain their native highlighting.
Supported plugins do not require this integration to render pages.

The tests/mode.test.mjs regression test uses the installed CodeMirror mode:
  node lib/plugins/codemirrorsyntax/tests/mode.test.mjs

